NAME

ulibGetGlobalSectionData - Returns message/file section information


SYNOPSIS

void ulibGetGlobalSectionData(long *MsgSections, long *FileSections,
                                       a0                a1

                              long **MsgList, long **FileList)
                                      a2             a3


DESCRIPTION

This function returns message section and file section information.

After this function returns, <MsgSections> and <FileSections> will point
to the number of configured message and file sections, respectively.

<MsgList> and <FileList> will point to an array of long integers, which are
the section numbers of the configured message and file sections.  Both lists
are ordered from lowest to highest.


NOTES

As with almost all xenolink.library functions, the Xenolink Manager must be
running for the values returned by this function to be valid.
